Author: Clarisse
Title: clareatsfood recipe finder
Last Update: May 15th, 2026
Purpose:
This project is a recipe finder that offers the user recipes based on the ingredients they have available in their pantry.
It allows users to select ingredients they have and reject ingredients they don't like.
Then, it calculates the recipes that best fit their selections.
All of the recipes offered are linked to my Food Instagram account (@clareatsfood), where I post easy reciped I've developed / Improved.

***NOTE ABOUT SLEEPOVER HOURS TRACKING***
I inadvertantly added two unrelated project files to my folder on my computer, so Hackatime is logging 7 hours 50 mins when it should be 5 hours 5o mins (it's logging 2 extra hours from my work on the unrelated files).

WHY I made this project: I wanted to sort my recipes with an easy-to-use recipe finder so my mom could
easily find a recipe when she's trying to use up a specific ingredient in the kitchen. If I ever decide
to take my passion for food more seriously, it's also a good porfolio piece to have.

HOW I made this project: I coded it in HTML/CSS/JS. No known bugs, but CSS was a struggle and may be wonky on mobile / different screen sizes.
AI was used in this project to format the recipes and their ingredients list into JSON, and sometimes to add the ingredient IDs to the ingredient div onclicks / oncontextmenus.
Photos are my own.
